{"3":[{"k":"p","t":"GAME SET-UP"},{"k":"p","t":"INTRODUCTION"},{"k":"p","t":"TAITO AMERICA\u2019S CRAZY CLIMBER UPRIGHT is a skill based video action game, with speech, designed for one or two players."},{"k":"p","t":"The object of the CRAZY CLIMBER game is to advance the climber to the top of each skyscraper attempting to avoid the various obstacles. A player can scale up to a total of four skyscrapers. A player accumulates point value for climbing and then receives these points if he is picked up by the helicopter at the top of each skyscraper. If the player misses the helicopter the bonus points are lost and the player advances to the next skyscraper. An additional climber is displayed if the players score reaches 30,000 points (adjustable) ."},{"k":"p","t":"GAME INSPECTION"},{"k":"p","t":"TAITO AMERICA\u2019S CRAZY CLIMBER game is ready to play when received. However, careful inspection is necessary to insure your game is in perfect condition. Please verify the following before turning the game on."},{"k":"li","t":"* Examine external parts for chips, dents, or broken parts."},{"k":"li","t":"* Open the service door and examine the following: Plug-in connectors to make sure they are firmly seated. Speaker Player controls. Printed circuit boards making sure there is no damage to the components."},{"k":"li","t":"* Check for loose foreign objects especially metal objects which may cause electrical problems. Fuses, making sure they are firmly in the holders. Transformer Coin Mechanisms"},{"k":"p","t":"If problems occur or technical assistance is required, contact our Customer Service Department HOT LINE Toll Free 800-323-0666 (except Illinois). Minois phone 981-1000 X 215."},{"k":"p","t":"The Video Monitor is properly adjusted before shipping, if there are any adjustments necessary refer to the manufacturers operating manual."},{"k":"p","t":"POWER REQUIREMENTS"},{"k":"p","t":"TAITO AMERICA\u2019S CRAZY CLIMBER game is shipped ready for operation at 120VAC, 60Hz with a power consumption of approximately 250 Watts."},{"k":"note","t":"CAUTION"},{"k":"p","t":"For sate operation it is recommended the cabinet be grounded. This game is equipped with a three conductor power cable. The third conductor is the ground conductor and when the cable is plugged into an appropriate receptable, the game is grounded. The offset pin on the power cable\u2019s three-prong connector is the ground connection."},{"k":"p","t":"LOCATION SPACE REQUIREMENTS"},{"k":"p","t":"Depth - 35\u201d (87.5cm) Width - 24\u201d (61cm) Height - 68\" (171cm) Weight - 300 Ibs. (135Kg) INSTALLATION REQUIREMENTS The following precautions should be followed when installing the game."},{"k":"li","t":"* Avoid rough handling of the game, the picture tube is fragile."},{"k":"li","t":"* Install the game on a level surface."},{"k":"li","t":"* Avoid installing the game where it may receive excessive sunlight or heat, to prevent the game from rising internal temperature."},{"k":"li","t":"* Do not install in a damp or dusty location."},{"k":"li","t":"* For a short time after connecting the power to the game, the picture may be temporarily distorted."},{"k":"p","t":"DIP SWITCH AND VOLUME CONTROL SETTINGS"},{"k":"p","t":"DIP SWITCH SETTINGS TAITO AMERICA\u2019S CRAZY CLIMBER game provides the following option switches. See Figure 8. These options can be found on PC Board \u201cA\u201d Switch B."},{"k":"p","t":"SW 1 and SW2 are used for selecting the number of climbers. Switches 1 and 2 are preset at the factory for 4 climbers."},{"k":"p","t":"CLIMBERS swt sw2 3 | OFF | OFF"},{"k":"tr","t":"4   ON   OFF"},{"k":"tr","t":"5   OFF   ON"},{"k":"tr","t":"6   ON   ON"},{"k":"p","t":"TABLE 1 CLIMBER OPTION"},{"k":"li","t":"* SW3 is used for adjusting the score at which time an additional climber is added. Switch 3 is preset at the factory for 30,000 points."},{"k":"p","t":"OFF 30,000 ON 50,000"},{"k":"p","t":"TABLE 2 CLIMBER SCORING OPTION"},{"k":"li","t":"* SW4 when in the ON position displays a test pattern and runs through four screens."},{"k":"li","t":"* SW5 & SW6 are used for coin selection. Switches 5 and 6 are preset at the factory for 1 coin - 1 play."},{"k":"tr","t":"COIN SELECTION   SWS   SWE"},{"k":"tr","t":"1 coin - 1 play   OFF   OFF"},{"k":"tr","t":"2 coin - 1 play   ON   OFF"},{"k":"tr","t":"3 coin - 1 play   OFF   ON"},{"k":"tr","t":"4 coin - 1 play   ON   ON"},{"k":"p","t":"TABLE 3 COIN SELECTION OPTION"},{"k":"li","t":"* SW7 & SW68 are normally in the OFF position uniess used for a free play. Then both switches should be in the ON position."},{"k":"note","t":"NOTE"},{"k":"p","t":"Switches must not be adjusted unless the power is off."},{"k":"p","t":"VOLUME CONTROL SETTING"},{"k":"li","t":"* VR. This option switch is used to contro! the volume. See Figure"},{"k":"li","t":"6. Volume goes down in turning as the arrow indicates."},{"k":"p","t":"MAINTENANCE All games require a certain amount of maintenance to keep them in good condition. A periodic check of mechanical controls would be beneficial to guarantee your game will be profitable."}],"5":[{"k":"p","t":"VIDEO AND CABINET ASSEMBLY"},{"k":"p","t":"TAITO"},{"k":"tr","t":"ITEM   PART NO.   DESCRIPTION   REFERENCE"},{"k":"tr","t":"1   47-00001-001 |Screened Acrylic Marquee Panel   400073"},{"k":"tr","t":"2   27-00001-001 |Fiuorescent Tube, Std., 15W   AA054711"},{"k":"tr","t":"3   42B-00057-001 |Fluorescent Lamp Panel   140006"},{"k":"tr","t":"4   26-00004-001 |Lamp Socket (Holder)   113000"},{"k":"tr","t":"5   61C-00007-001 |Glass Stop Bracket   500024"},{"k":"tr","t":"6   26-00005-001 |Starter Socket   114001"},{"k":"tr","t":"7   29-06003-001 | Starter   114000"},{"k":"tr","t":"8   18-00002-002 [Ballast Transformer   010006"},{"k":"tr","t":"9   61B-0001 1-001 |\u2018'L\u201d\u2019 Bracket   AA013584"},{"k":"tr","t":"10   04-00008-001 |Cabinet Assembly   860007"},{"k":"tr","t":"\"   63B-00006-001 |T Moiding, Chrome   400007"},{"k":"tr","t":"12   59-00008-001 |Clamp Fastener   390002"},{"k"